{
  "tema": 5157,
  "slug": "futuro-haber",
  "titulo": "Conjugate haber in the simple future",
  "subtitulo": "Habrá: there will be. And habré, habrás… for the future perfect.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "Haber has the future stem habr-: habré, habrás, habrá, habremos, habrán. Habrá alone means there will be.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Haber** is irregular in the simple future because its stem is **habr-**. The endings are the regular future ones."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**habr-**",
            "**-é, -ás, -á, -emos, -án**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "haber"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "habré"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "habrás"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "habrá"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "habremos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "habrán"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Used **on its own**, only **habrá** appears: it's the future of **hay** and means _there will be_. It never goes plural: **habrá tres personas**, not **habrán**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "All the forms are used with a past participle to build the **future perfect**: **habré hecho** (_I will have done_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **hay** today, **habrá** tomorrow. One word for one thing or a hundred."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Habrá== inundaciones en invierno.",
              "en": "There will be floods in winter."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Habrá== un profe nuevo en septiembre.",
              "en": "There will be a new teacher in September."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Habrá== banda en la boda?",
              "en": "Will there be a band at the wedding?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Habrá== tres hombres y dos mujeres en la junta.",
              "en": "There will be three men and two women at the meeting."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mañana ==habrá== buenas olas en Baja Malibú.",
              "en": "There will be good waves at Baja Malibu tomorrow."
            },
            {
              "es": "Para las seis, yo ==habré hecho== la comida.",
              "en": "By six, I will have made lunch."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
